# K8s Security -
- A container is a process running on a Linux system. That process has an identity and permissions.

For example, on a Linux machine, we have:

User
  ↓
Permissions
  ↓
What the process is allowed to do

Kubernetes Security Context allows us to control these things for containers.

          apiVersion: v1
          kind: Pod
          metadata:
            name: wepod
          spec:
            containers:
            - name: busybox
              image: busybox
              command: ["sleep", "3200"]
              securityContext:
                capabilities:
                  add: ["SYS_TIME"]



  
